.TH labctl 1 "October 2026" "linux-labs" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
labctl \- start, grade and reset hands-on Linux labs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B labctl
.I COMMAND
.RI [ LAB ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B labctl
runs the hands-on Linux labs provided by the linux-labs package.
It prepares a lab, shows its task, grades the final state and resets the
system afterwards.
Labs are installed under
.IR /opt/linux-labs/labs .
Only one lab is active at a time; the active lab is recorded in
.I /opt/linux-labs/.current_lab
and shown as
.B [LAB:<name>]
in the shell prompt.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI start " LAB"
Prepare the system for the lab, mark it as the active lab and print its
task. Requires root; the
.B student
user can run it through
.BR sudo .
If the lab setup fails, the lab is not started and labctl exits with the
setup exit status.
.TP
.BI task " LAB"
Print the task of the lab again: the header line, the category and level
line and the task text. It does not change the system and does not need
root.
.TP
.BI grade " LAB"
Check the current state of the system against the lab criteria. Each
criterion is printed on one line with the result PASS or FAIL, followed by
the overall result and the number of criteria met.
.TP
.BI reset " LAB"
Undo the lab setup and the changes the solution makes, and clear the active
lab. Requires root.
.TP
.B list
List the installed labs with their objective.
.TP
.BI solution " LAB"
Show the reference solution of the lab. Uses
.B less
when standard output is a terminal.
.TP
.BI configure " ACTION"
Configure the lab environment (network, nodes for multi-node labs).
.I ACTION
is one of
.BR interactive ,
.BR list ,
.B set
.IR "KEY VALUE" ,
.B validate
or
.BR reset .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo labctl start files-04
labctl task files-04
labctl grade files-04
labctl solution files-04
sudo labctl reset files-04
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B labctl grade
exits 0 when all criteria are met and 1 otherwise.
.B labctl start
and
.B labctl reset
exit 0 on success.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value, the grading output is not coloured. Colour
is used only when standard output is a terminal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/linux-labs/labs/
Installed labs.
.TP
.I /opt/linux-labs/.current_lab
Name of the active lab.
.TP
.I /etc/linux-labs/config
System-wide configuration; otherwise
.I ~/.config/linux-labs/config
is used.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sudo (8)
.SH AUTHORS
linux-labs maintainers.
